  "notes": "FORMS:\n{封|ふう} (seal) + {鎖|さ} (chain, lock). Used as both a noun and suru-verb.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {道路|どうろ}{封鎖|ふうさ}: road blockade\n- {国境|こっきょう}{封鎖|ふうさ}: border closure\n- {都市|とし}{封鎖|ふうさ}: city lockdown\n- {口座|こうざ}{封鎖|ふうさ}: account freeze\n- {経済|けいざい}{封鎖|ふうさ}: economic blockade\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{封鎖|ふうさ}する: to seal off/block ~\n- {封鎖|ふうさ}が{解除|かいじょ}される: the blockade is lifted\n\nUSAGE:\nGained wider everyday usage during pandemic discussions as the Japanese equivalent of \"lockdown,\" though the loanword ロックダウン is also used. Traditionally associated with military blockades, police cordons, and border closures.",
